WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.800
&gt;&gt; At Xbox, we have

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:04.515
a controller design
that our fans love.

00:00:04.515 --> 00:00:05.850
However, for gamers with

00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:07.390
limited mobility or gamers

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:09.020
who don't use both their hands,

00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.520
this controller design
might not work best for them.

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:16.575
&gt;&gt; Doorknobs are
the worst thing ever invented.

00:00:16.575 --> 00:00:19.600
Putting on shoes, the
cell phones that I use.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.390
These are the sorts of
things that we don't

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:23.220
think about until we have to,

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:25.840
and I think about them every day.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:30.285
&gt;&gt; I have cerebral palsy
in my entire right side.

00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:33.630
This side of
the controller is fine,

00:00:33.630 --> 00:00:37.200
this side doesn't happen.

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:39.594
As game platforms have
gotten more sophisticated,

00:00:39.594 --> 00:00:41.940
the controllers have
gotten more sophisticated,

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:44.590
and it started to get
really frustrating.

00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.300
&gt;&gt; We designed the Xbox
Adaptive Controller through

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:51.045
feedback from the
accessibility community.

00:00:51.045 --> 00:00:54.210
&gt;&gt; The Xbox Adaptive
Controller is really easy,

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:56.685
you just plug it in and

00:00:56.685 --> 00:01:00.780
then you can plug in
other various devices.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.935
I can make it work for
me the way it has to.

00:01:04.935 --> 00:01:06.915
&gt;&gt; With the Xbox
Adaptive Controller,

00:01:06.915 --> 00:01:09.150
a gamer can game with one hand,

00:01:09.150 --> 00:01:12.030
and one foot, or one hand
and their shoulder,

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.830
or even one foot and their chin.

00:01:13.830 --> 00:01:16.360
&gt;&gt; And I can change
it from game to game.

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:19.845
&gt;&gt; Good, ready? Forward,

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:22.230
squeeze tall, there it is.

00:01:22.230 --> 00:01:23.980
&gt;&gt; Craig Hospital is

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:25.450
a facility for patients

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.040
who've either had
a spinal cord injury,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:28.510
or a traumatic brain injury,

00:01:28.510 --> 00:01:30.890
and it's a place for their rehab.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.580
&gt;&gt; We're here for a game night,
and we're helping

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:35.170
new patients getting back

00:01:35.170 --> 00:01:36.260
into gaming again.
Is that the D-pad?

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:36.390
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.360
&gt;&gt; Our role as

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:41.700
occupational therapists is to
get people back to doing.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.770
When the Xbox Adaptive
Controller came

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.755
along, it acted like an Xbox
controller and it just worked.

00:01:46.755 --> 00:01:48.790
&gt;&gt; It's over there.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:53.755
&gt;&gt; On the Standard Xbox
Controller is just

00:01:53.755 --> 00:01:55.605
hard to press
the buttons because I

00:01:55.605 --> 00:01:57.600
can't really put
pressure through my hands,

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.850
but then with
the adaptive controller,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.710
I can use larger joysticks,

00:02:01.710 --> 00:02:03.855
larger buttons that are
easier to press and reach.

00:02:03.855 --> 00:02:06.315
&gt;&gt; Cory and his brother
Zachary are twins.

00:02:06.315 --> 00:02:07.975
Before Corey's injuries, Zachary

00:02:07.975 --> 00:02:09.450
had gamed with him regularly,

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:10.695
and that was the way that they

00:02:10.695 --> 00:02:12.485
related to each
other as siblings.

00:02:12.485 --> 00:02:14.090
&gt;&gt; Who do you love playing Xbox

00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:16.045
with here
at Craig Hospital?

00:02:16.045 --> 00:02:17.640
&gt;&gt; Zak.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:19.680
&gt;&gt; The Xbox Adaptive Controller,

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:21.185
and the co-pilot feature,

00:02:21.185 --> 00:02:23.350
allowed them again to
play games together.

00:02:23.350 --> 00:02:25.760
So, there's a huge
social component to it.

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:26.625
&gt;&gt; We've got it.

00:02:26.625 --> 00:02:28.035
&gt;&gt; Yes.

00:02:28.035 --> 00:02:30.695
&gt;&gt; They can play
any game they want.

00:02:30.695 --> 00:02:34.670
I see the confidence
just burst out of them.

00:02:43.842 --> 00:02:44.842
[XBOX SOUND]

